Local changes to isocline 1.1.0 from Hackage (MIT, Daan Leijen):
- src/tty_esc.c: parse xterm modifyOtherKeys, ESC [ 27 ; mods ; key ~, which
  kitty, WezTerm and Ghostty send for Shift+Enter. Unpatched, isocline stops
  after two parameters and prints "13~".
- isocline.cabal, test/: drop the example executable and test suite, so
  hilda's `cabal build all` and `tests: True` do not build them.
Delete vendor/ once an upstream release parses the sequence.

